WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.036
HOST: Bladesmiths,
congratulations.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.537
You've made it to the final
round of this competition.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.272
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:12.245
to recreate an iconic weapon
from history, the war golok.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.483
Originating in the Philippines
during the 16th century,

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.785
the war golok featured a
straight, double-edged blade

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:21.086
with no tip.

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:22.521
Due to the Spanish
occupation at the time,

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:25.125
Filipinos were outlawed
from having pointed swords,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.628
and the blade was often used for
vegetation and chopping wood.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:32.064
However, by the Philippine
Revolution in 1896,

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:34.334
Filipinos adapted to
the tipless weapon,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.136
and it became a weapon of war.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.005
It was so effective in battle
it inspired later variations

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.040
of the weapon, such as
the British military's

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.910
army golok in the early 1950s.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:44.911
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.279
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.918
MATT WAGNER: My
name is Matt Wagner.

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:54.354
I run an auto body
restoration shop,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.523 line:14%
and I work with metal every day.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.124 line:8%
I started watching
"Forged in Fire,"

00:00:59.224 --> 00:01:01.160
and then one day I was
like, you know what?

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.661
I think I can do that.

00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:04.597
I'm ready to crank this baby up.

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:08.868
I'm anxious because I've
never made a sword this long.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.137
I want to win this
competition because I've

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.407
always thought I was meant
to do something better.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.543
Today is a make
or break it point.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.780
My main concern is quenching
the blade because that

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:24.217
could create massive warping.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.618
This is the big moment.

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:30.923
Ha, ha, ha!

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.392
It's fricking straight.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.094
So now that I'm
quenched, I'd like

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.696
to take a couple whacks
at a piece of wood just

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:39.232
to see what's going to happen.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:49.842
[bleep] I shattered my
blade into three pieces.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.077
This is an epic failure.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:54.080
I'm running out of time.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:56.382
I'm going to have to start over.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.250
I might not finish this thing.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.653
My plan is to use a
piece of leaf spring

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.290
and get a complete sword
forged out in one day.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.059
I'm working on a
deadly timeline,

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:11.231
and I am just
busting my [bleep]..

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.532
I've got to get my quench
done by the end of day four

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.335
because I don't know if
I have a good blade yet.

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:17.970
I may have to build
another one tomorrow.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:18.904
You never know.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.105
It's cooling pretty quick.

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:22.008
I'm running out of time.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.244
If this blade doesn't
harden with this quench,

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.944
I'm really screwed.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:27.380
I've got my fingers crossed.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.151
We've got a hard blade.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.486
I am super happy.

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:36.989
Looks like I'm going to have
something for the big show.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.558 line:14%
[laughs]

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.127
BRIAN SCHMIDT: My
name is Brian Schmidt.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.097 line:8%
I believe my great-grandfather
was a blacksmith.

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.567
So when I saw
"Forged in Fire," I

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.302
wanted to try and
make my own blades

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.570
and just create
memories with my family.

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.040
I think I have a pretty
good chance of winning.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.843
The basic shape of my
blade is in there now.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.878
This is going to
be the war golok.

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:00.246
The blade's looking really nice.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:03.916
I've got the handle set up
for a lot of work today.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:05.484
The handle's made out of maple.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:08.387
It's also the part of the
knife where I'm customizing

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.223
it for myself a little bit.

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.423
Yeah, not so bad.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.593
I think they turned
out pretty nice.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.095
I sharpened my
blade three times.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.864
That thing's razor sharp.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.098
All right.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:20.666
Feels good.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:24.603
Now I want to go test the
blade, and my son is joining me.

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:25.304
Ready?

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.907
All right, here we go.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.976
 Ooh, awesome.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.745
 That thing slices
right through.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.748
Feels good in my hand, so I
think it's going to do well.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:36.516
All right.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.183
 Very deadly.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.285
 Bladesmiths, to see
what kind of lethal damage

00:03:40.385 --> 00:03:42.288
your weapon will do,
we'll take your sword

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:46.092
and deliver hacks and
slashes on this pig carcass.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.026
Brian, you're up first.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:47.726
You ready for this?

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:49.128
 Absolutely.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.463
Depending on where you
hit that blade, you know,

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.565
it can always snap apart.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.701
 Bladesmiths,
unfortunately I am still

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.336
recovering from an injury.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:04:00.272
So Anthony, one of my senior
instructors from Marcaida Kali,

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:04.010
will be the butcher
to your pork chop.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:04.943
[music playing]

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.246
 Nice.

00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:14.520
Phew.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.558
 All right, Brian, let's
talk about your blade.

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:22.395
First up, your edge
is razor sharp.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:25.898
It lacerated easily through
bones, through the spine.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.969
The one issue here is that
you have a very blocky handle.

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.638
Aside from that, it will kill.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.172
Good job.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.239
 Thanks.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:35.874
 Matt, ready to chop?

00:04:35.974 --> 00:04:36.842
 I've been ready.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.677
 Let's do this.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.347
[music playing]

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:55.494
OK, Matt, its balance and weight
is very forward for a chopper,

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:59.165
but your edge is sharp enough
to lacerate into the carcass.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.800
It did chop the spine.

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:02.701
It did chop bone.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.570
This will kill.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:05.405
 Thank you.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:11.177
 Gentlemen, this is
the strength test.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.246
To test the strength and
durability of your edge,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.448
I'm going to chop into
these huge logs 10 times.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:19.385
Remember, this test is all about
what happens to your weapons

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.286
and not what
happens to the logs.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:22.120
Brian, you're up first.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:22.955
Are you ready?

00:05:23.021 --> 00:05:24.023
 I think so, yeah.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:24.957
 All right.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:28.594
[music playing]

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:50.249
 Made it.

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:53.185
 Well, Brian, your
edge held up perfectly.

00:05:53.251 --> 00:05:56.155
There's no bending, no warping.

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.390
It's still razor sharp
all the way down.

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.726
Man, it was fun to swing.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.293
Well done.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.227
 Thank you.

00:06:02.327 --> 00:06:02.995
 Matt, you're up.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:03.796
You ready?

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:04.397
 Give it a try.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:05.931
JUDGE: All right.

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:09.001
[music playing]

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:25.218
 Ah.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.653
 Well, Matt, there's
so much forward weight

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:30.723
that it actually bent that way.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.859
On the plus side, your
edge held up beautifully.

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:35.628
I mean, there's no problems
with that edge at all.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:43.636
It's still very sharp, but this
S bend in it, it's significant.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:46.038
 Bladesmiths, you both
brought in some pretty

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:48.440
extraordinary historic weapons.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.009
But in this arena
of competition,

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.078
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.583
Brian, congratulations.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:00.686
You are the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:01.954
 Thank you.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.190
 Matt, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.991
JUDGE: Matt, your
blade is impressive.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.193
We saw that it could kill.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.028 line:8%
But unfortunately,
in the strength test,

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:11.897 line:8%
it took a significant bend,
and it's for that reason

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:13.399
we have to let you go.

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:14.600
 I understand.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.770
 Matt, please
surrender your golok.

00:07:17.836 --> 00:07:20.806
MATT WAGNER: Even with
losing, at the end of the day,

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:24.143
I don't feel like I really
lost because I went way

00:07:24.209 --> 00:07:26.378
further than I ever expected.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:29.048
I don't know enough
about it yet that I

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:30.649
can make that perfect blade.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.919
So, you know, I'll
keep learning.

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:38.490
 Brian, you are the new
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:41.159
and that comes with
a check for $10,000.

00:07:41.259 --> 00:07:42.161
Good job.
[applause]

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:42.961
 Thank you, guys.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.529
Thank you.

00:07:44.629 --> 00:07:47.066
 Please present your
weapon to the judges.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.435
BRIAN SCHMIDT: It feels great
to be a "Forged in Fire" champ.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:50.903
Can't believe I won.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:51.904
It's awesome.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.639
I would say if
somebody wants to start

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.307
learning how to
make a knife, start

00:07:55.373 --> 00:07:56.375
out watching "Forged in Fire."

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:57.743
Just start at episode one.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.276
Binge watch.

00:07:58.377 --> 00:08:02.148
[music playing]

